---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Applications & Solved NCERT Word Problems | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Master real-world NCERT word problems involving clock minute hands, car wipers, umbrella ribs, and brooch designs for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/areas-related-to-circles" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Areas Related to Circles</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">03</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 03 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Applications & Solved <span>NCERT Word Problems</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master real-world NCERT word problems involving clock minute hands, car wipers, umbrella ribs, and brooch designs step by step with diagrams.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · GENERAL APPROACH -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · REAL WORLD CONCEPTS</div>
					<h2>Key Real-World Angle Rules</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Clock Minute Hand</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Minute Hand Speed</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">Moves 360° in 60 minutes ⟹ <strong>6° per minute</strong>. In 5 minutes, θ = 5 × 6° = <strong>30°</strong>.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Car Wipers</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Dual Car Wipers</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">Total area swept by 2 non-overlapping wipers = <strong>2 × [(θ / 360°) × πr²]</strong>.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Umbrella Ribs</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Equal Sectors</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">If an umbrella has 8 equal ribs, central angle for 1 sector = <strong>360° / 8 = 45°</strong>.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1 · CLOCK MINUTE HAND</span>
							<h3>The length of the minute hand of a clock is 14 cm. Find the area swept by the minute hand in 5 minutes.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<!-- SVG Diagram -->
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="340" height="230" viewBox="0 0 340 230" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
									<!-- Clock Outer Face (Center 170, 115, radius 80) -->
									<circle cx="170" cy="115" r="80" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="3.5" fill="#ffffff"/>

									<!-- Swept Sector (30° from 12 o'clock (170, 35) to 1 o'clock (210, 46)) -->
									<path d="M 170,115 L 170,35 A 80 80 0 0 1 210,46 Z" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Minute Hand at 12 (Initial) -->
									<line x1="170" y1="115" x2="170" y2="35" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="3"/>
									<!-- Minute Hand at 1 (5 mins later) -->
									<line x1="170" y1="115" x2="210" y2="46" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="3"/>

									<!-- Center Point -->
									<circle cx="170" cy="115" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>

									<!-- Angle Arc 30° -->
									<path d="M 170 80 A 35 35 0 0 1 187 85" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
									<text x="175" y="72" fill="#dc2626" font-size="12" font-weight="900">30°</text>

									<!-- Clock Ticks -->
									<text x="165" y="28" fill="#0f172a" font-size="12" font-weight="900">12</text>
									<text x="218" y="42" fill="#0f172a" font-size="12" font-weight="900">1</text>
									<text x="242" y="78" fill="#0f172a" font-size="12" font-weight="900">2</text>

									<!-- Labels -->
									<text x="145" y="80" fill="#2563eb" font-size="12" font-weight="800">r = 14 cm</text>
									<text x="195" y="105" fill="#1d4ed8" font-size="12" font-weight="900">Area Swept in 5 mins</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<p>In 60 minutes, minute hand rotates 360°. In 5 minutes, θ = (360° / 60) × 5 = <strong>30°</strong>.</p>
							<p>Radius <em>r = 14 cm</em>.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Area = (30° / 360°) × (22/7) × 14 × 14<br/>
								Area = (1 / 12) × 22 × 2 × 14 = (22 × 28) / 12 = <strong>154 / 3 = 51.33 cm²</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2 · CAR WIPERS</span>
							<h3>A car has two wipers which do not overlap. Each wiper has a blade of length 25 cm sweeping through an angle of 115°. Find total area cleaned at each sweep.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Given: blade length <em>r = 25 cm</em>, angle <em>θ = 115°</em>, number of wipers = 2.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Area by 1 Wiper = (115° / 360°) × (22/7) × 25 × 25<br/>
								Total Area (2 Wipers) = 2 × (115° / 360°) × (22/7) × 625<br/>
								Total Area = (230 / 360) × (22/7) × 625 = <strong>158125 / 126 = 1254.96 cm²</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Minute hand rotates <strong>6° per minute</strong> (360° in 60 mins).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Always multiply single sector area by the number of blades/ribs when applicable.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Keep exact fractions (e.g. 154/3 cm²) for board exams unless decimal is specified.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/areas-related-to-circles/segment-of-a-circle" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Area of Segment</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/areas-related-to-circles/pyqs" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">AREAS RELATED TO CIRCLES</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 03 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 75%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/areas-related-to-circles/perimeter-area-sector" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Perimeter & Sector Area</strong>
									<small>Arc length & sector area</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/areas-related-to-circles/segment-of-a-circle" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Area of Segment</strong>
									<small>Minor & major segments</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/areas-related-to-circles/applications-and-practice" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Applications & Practice</strong>
									<small>NCERT word problems</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/areas-related-to-circles/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

	<style>
		.lesson-page {
			min-height: 100vh;
			background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f8fbff 0%, #ffffff 35%, #f7f9fc 100%);
			color: #14213d;
			padding: 45px 0 100px;
		}

		.lesson-container {
			width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 40px));
			margin: 0 auto;
		}

		.back-link {
			display: inline-flex;
			align-items: center;
			gap: 7px;
			color: #667085;
			text-decoration: none;
			font-size: 14px;
			font-weight: 700;
			margin-bottom: 35px;
			transition: color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
		}

		.back-link:hover {
			color: #2563eb;
			transform: translateX(-3px);
		}

		.lesson-header {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 80px minmax(0, 1fr);
			gap: 25px;
			align-items: center;
			padding: 40px;
			border: 1px solid #e1e7f0;
			border-radius: 24px;
			background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
			box-shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(20, 33, 61, 0.055);
			margin-bottom: 45px;
		}

		.lesson-number {
